          "line": 41,
          "text": " * Atomic file guarantees file integrity by ensuring that a file has been completely written and"
        },
        {
          "line": 42,
          "text": " * sync'd to disk before renaming it to the original file. Previously this is done by renaming the"
        },
        {
          "line": 43,
          "text": " * original file to a backup file beforehand, but this approach couldn't handle the case where the"
        },
        {
          "line": 44,
          "text": " * file is created for the first time. This class will also handle the backup file created by the"
        },
        {
          "line": 45,
          "text": " * old implementation properly."
        },
        {
          "line": 46,
          "text": " * <p>"
        },
        {
          "line": 47,
          "text": " * Atomic file does not confer any file locking semantics. Do not use this class when the file may"
        },
        {
          "line": 48,
          "text": " * be accessed or modified concurrently by multiple threads or processes. The caller is responsible"
        },
        {
          "line": 49,
          "text": " * for ensuring appropriate mutual exclusion invariants whenever it accesses the file."
        },
        {
          "line": 50,
          "text": " */"
        },
